      },
      "message": "feat(app): refusal ghost for part-way refusals, ghost-aware match sites, ground-aware ghost colour\n\nGenerators that refuse part-way now hand back the moves they had built,\nas a display-only ghost (GenError::with_ghost_moves over a builder's\nmoves): 2D contour (control-comp lead and span refusals), bore and\ncircular (per-hole/ring pass budget), trochoidal slot (level emit,\ncrossed loops), the 3-D ladder's adaptive level plan, plasma profile\n(per-contour, cover/kerf laws, torch spans), probing, turning form and\ngroove. Every adoption is a map_err on an error path; successful output\nis unchanged and the CL/NC goldens are byte-identical. The rest are\nlisted with their reason in docs/decisions/871-refusal-ghost-rest.md.\n\ncross_spindle::in_world rewrites a Ghosted refusal's sentence, spot and\nmoves by the spindle shift (dropping the ghost when it cannot carry it);\npicks::door_refusal reads a Ghosted refusal's words like the plain one;\nbody_judged::name_enclosure goes through map_msg so a ghost keeps its\nholder words.\n\nThe ghost colour takes #698's ground-aware dimming: the dark ground is\nunchanged, a light ground fades toward itself, the cutting tone clearing\n3:1 on the light viewport in every colour-vision palette.\n\nFixes #871\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
