        "date": "2026-11-12T03:22:27Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app): refusal ghost where a frame map or a merge came first\n\nThe part-way refusals #871 left owed now hand back their partial path in\nthe frame of the path the generator returns, so it lands where the part\nis once run_job maps that frame:\n\n- finishing3d raster/rings/swarf_multi carry the moves built so far;\n  Rotary Contour/Parallel carry that ghost (and the radial relink's) out\n  through the same pose law and world exit as the path (rotary::to_world)\n- the 5-axis stamp's shank refusal carries the world plan before its\n  move; the swarf link laws, the curve walk, the rotary C gate, the\n  fixture route and the cross drill's part law carry the world path\n- the cross drill's rapids/holder laws carry the spindle-frame chain\n  back by the spindle shift\n- nested refusals (pocket3d air split, rest ladder, stitched contour\n  runs) put the outer moves in front of the inner ghost\n  (GenError::after_moves / Ghost::after)\n\nSuccess paths are untouched. The sites left without a ghost, with\nreasons, are in docs/decisions/1015-ghost-frames.md. Face under an area\nturn is handled by #1023.\n\nFixes #1015\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
